   DuelField.tsx for how each row's leading empty cell(s) work. (9 is the
   widest row's own column count: 1 leading empty cell + field + 5
   Monster Zones + grave + banished = 8 zone entries, +1.)

   grid-template-columns and gap are no longer set here — each of the 8
   gaps between columns is now independently controllable (see
   columnGaps.ts), so DuelField.tsx computes gridTemplateColumns itself
   (widening each column's own track by that gap, with the row's own CSS
   `gap` left at 0) and applies it as an inline style on every
   .DuelField-row div, rather than this one static rule setting a single
   uniform gap for all of them.

   The individual gaps between columns holding a Monster Zone or
   Spell/Trap Zone on at least one side need to stay at ~36px or more —
   the Defense Position rotated overlay on those zones overhangs each
   zone's normal 72px width by a good margin on either side (a rotated
   105x72 box vs the zone's own 72x105), so a smaller gap there would let
   two neighboring zones' overlays visually touch or overlap. See
   columnGaps.ts's own comments for exactly which gaps those are. */
.DuelField-row {
